    "narrative": "The engine is firing on all cylinders today, led by **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, who boasts the day\u2019s highest projection at 81.07. His matchup against Singer is ideal, bolstered by a significant 40-PA BvP historical edge and favorable hitting conditions that cement him as our clear cornerstone. **Cal Raleigh** (76.47) and **Daulton Varsho** (72.31) also provide elite value, with **Cal Raleigh** benefiting immensely from a soft matchup against the 5.30 xERA of Lauer, while **Daulton Varsho** leverages a strong platoon advantage against the right-handed Littell. We are also leaning on **Gleyber Torres** (67.52) in the leadoff spot; his synergy with a platoon-heavy matchup against Rogers makes him a high-efficiency play despite the inherent volatility of the top of the order.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Luis Arraez**, who fell just shy of our 40.0 floor with a 38.98 rating. While his contact profile is usually a staple, he is being neutralized by a matchup against Pannone, whose elite suppression skills (0.00 xERA) created too much risk to justify the start. Conversely, we are keeping a close watch on **Lawrence Butler** (49.84) and **Masyn Winn** (45.83); both are currently projected for the lineup, but their final standing is subject to \"Lineup Pending\" status. **Taylor Ward** faces a significant test against Skubal, a genuine ace, but his role as leadoff and the platoon edge keep him marginally playable at 53.36. We are prioritizing efficiency across the board to navigate the 5x5 categories, holding **Brendan Donovan**, **JJ Bleday**, and **Zack Gelof** in reserve as we monitor weather risks and late-scratches that could force a rotation into the active lineup.",
